        <h2 id="workflow">
          A Simple Workflow for Sellers and Creators
        </h2>

        <h3>
          1. Calculate before pricing
        </h3>

        <p>
          Estimate relevant costs before choosing a final
          selling or service price. This gives you a clearer
          picture of your potential margin.
        </p>

        <h3>
          2. Compare realistic scenarios
        </h3>

        <p>
          Test more than one price when possible. Comparing
          different scenarios can show how changes in price
          affect your estimated earnings or profit.
        </p>

        <h3>
          3. Include your real costs
        </h3>

        <p>
          Platform calculations are only one part of the
          picture. Your actual business costs may also include
          inventory, shipping, refunds, advertising, software,
          taxes, and your time.
        </p>

        <h3>
          4. Customize generated ideas
        </h3>

        <p>
          If you use a title generator, treat the suggestions
          as a starting point. Adjust them so the final title
          accurately represents your actual content.
        </p>


